+# GitHub workflow dispatch examples
+
+This file contains example payloads and commands to dispatch the "Run Production Proofs" workflow using either curl (GitHub API) or the gh CLI.
+
+1) curl (GitHub API) example (replace OWNER, REPO, WORKFLOW_FILENAME and set GITHUB_TOKEN):
+
+curl -X POST \
+  -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer $GITHUB_TOKEN" \
+  https://api.github.com/repos/OWNER/REPO/actions/workflows/run_production_proofs.yml/dispatches \
+  -d '{
+    "ref": "main",
+    "inputs": {
+      "evidence_bucket": "s3://aegis-evidence-prod",
+      "confirm": "RUN_PROOFS",
+      "promote_gatekeeper": "no"
+    }
+  }'
+
+2) gh CLI example:
+
+gh workflow run "Run Production Proofs" -R OWNER/REPO --field evidence_bucket="s3://aegis-evidence-prod" --field confirm=RUN_PROOFS --field promote_gatekeeper=no
+
+Notes:
+- The workflow filename and workflow name must match what is present in the repo.
+- The environment must have appropriate kubeconfig and secrets if the workflow applies resources to cluster.
+
